  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps` only. The mill post `tormach.cps` does not change.\n\nLinuxCNC's G30 moves every axis in one straight line to the stored position (params 5181-5189). The operator stores that position, so the post cannot know where the line goes. Before this change, the first rapid after `G30` went diagonally to the start point, and the closing `G30` went diagonally from the last retract. Now:\n\n- **After G30** (tool change, or a \"home\" after-operation), the first point is approached one axis at a time:\n  - The point is outside the stock's diameter (all turning and threading starts): `G0 X`, then `G0 Z`.\n  - The point is inside the diameter, in front of the face (a hole on centre): `G0 Z`, then `G0 X`. A point ON the face goes to the section's `ClearancePlane` first, then X, then Z down to the point.\n  - Any other point: refused by name.\n- **Before G30** (tool change, \"home\", program end): `G0 X` out to the stock's diameter, then `G0 Z` out to the face (or to the `ClearancePlane` when the corner is not clear in either axis). The lines go before the next section's notes and work offset word, because they are in the old frame.\n- **Stock and planes** come from the stream's own `StockXY*`, `StockZTop` and `ClearancePlane` PARAMs. No margin is added by the post.\n- **Refused by name:** no stock box; a first point inside the stock with no `ClearancePlane` in front of the face; a section that ends inside the stock's envelope; a section that ends on the stock's corner with no `ClearancePlane`; a feed, arc or thread half-turn as the first motion after G30.\n\n**Order chosen:** X first, then Z, for every point outside the stock's diameter. For a hole on centre, X first from a G30 beside the bar moves into the bar, and a clearance diameter is not stated in the stream. Z first to the stated `ClearancePlane` needs no guess, so the post uses it there. The reasons are in `docs/decisions/1604-lathe-g30-rapid.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/lathe_post_tormach_g30.rs` (each pin mutation-checked; seven mutations of the post, each one fails at least one pin):\n\n- `the_first_move_after_g30_is_x_alone_then_z_alone`: turning and G76 threading programs go `G0 X..` then `G0 Z..` after each G30; the hole goes `G0 Z30`, `G0 X0`, `G0 Z20`.\n- `the_departure_goes_plus_x_then_plus_z_before_g30`: the hole ends `G0 X20` before G30; a section behind the face leaves `G0 Z10` before the next tool change, before the next work offset word.\n- `no_stored_g30_outside_the_stock_is_reached_across_it`: for a 41 x 41 grid of stored G30 positions outside the stock, no G30 line and no added rapid crosses the stock (turning, hole and thread programs). The first move from every G30 is one axis, and every G30 line starts at the stock's outer corner.\n- `a_missing_stock_or_clearance_is_refused_by_name`: no stock, no clearance plane in front of the face, an end on the corner with no clearance, an end inside the envelope, and a feed first after G30.\n\nMutations: radial approach Z-then-X; the old diagonal approach; no departure; departure without +Z; departure without +X; no clearance refusal; no stock refusal.\n\n**Goldens:** the eight `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/*.nc` and the recorded `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/tormach-lathe/tool_change.nc` were regenerated. A script checked each diff: the first two-axis `G0` after each `G30` becomes one-axis `G0` lines that end at the same point; the lines added before a `G30` are one-axis `+X` or `+Z` moves; every other line is the same and in the same order. Result: GOLDEN DIFF OK (12 approaches split, 5 departures added). I also mutated a golden two ways (a changed F word, a changed end point) and the script failed both.\n\nHand-built test streams in `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread` and `lathe_cycle_exit` now state a stock (`tormach_lathe_support::stock_params`), because the post refuses a stream with no stock. Two assertions changed to the split approach (`G0 X12.1\\nG0 Z14`), and the G76 drive-line test reads the last X before the G76 block.\n\nGates on head `9acdd7e8`: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (post suites ok 24 s, app suites ok 1188 s, 0 failed; the changed recorded golden pulls in every post and app suite). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **No PathPilot lathe Hub run was done.** A PathPilot lathe Hub run of the turning, thread and hole programs is wanted, with G30 stored (a) on centre in front of the face and (b) beside the bar behind the face.\n- A box stock turned on a lathe: the post uses the box's largest half-width, not its half-diagonal, because the stream does not say if the stock is round. Filed as #1666 (P3).\n- The idle tools of a gang plate: the post knows only the active tool's control point.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Open drafts #517, #518 and #468 also change `tormach-lathe.cps` in its G76 sections. This PR touches only one line there (the G76 drive-line rapid goes through the new approach after G30). Whichever PR merges second refreshes from main.\n- Fork synced at v0.18.0 (process files at upstream PROCESS_VERSION); this branch is from `upstream/main`.\n\nChangelog: Tormach lathe post: after G30 the first point is approached one axis at a time (X then Z outside the stock's diameter, Z then X in front of the face), and before each G30 the tool leaves +X to the stock's diameter, then +Z to the face; a missing stock or clearance plane is refused by name (#1604)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1604\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
